youkan's NetHack brass
(http://www11.cds.ne.jp/~youkan/nethack/index_e.html) is not credible!
It's got a load of stuff that I completely wasn't expecting from a
demi-variant that has not really been talked about at all here. Like:

* The Material patch (in which, among other things, silver, bronze and
mithril versions of ANY metallic object can be easily generated)
* Monsters with steeds! (in which monsters ride steeds! Double whoo!)
* Swamp and dead tree terrain! (The first being pleasantly similar to
my shallow water terrain patch...)
* Robbing enemies, menu-style!
* More random level varieties, such as ice caves, ghost towns and
forests!
* Autotargeting for polearms!
* Water elementals with drowning attacks!
* Some stuff from NetHack+ that got put into SLASH before Kevin Hugo
went and balanced it out of existence.
* Some manga-styled function in which female characters dressing up as
maids or nurses somehow get super powers! (In one word: <(o_O)>)

And, um, plenty of internal tweaks that I haven't mentioned. However,
much of the big stuff up here appears to be underdeveloped, or at least
not quite exploring its full potential. But for a patchwriter like me,
what's there is nothing short of mouth-watering. Hedonism aside, right
now I spent most of today porting the Monsteed functionality into a
vanilla patch:

http://www.greyfire.org/~l/monsteed.diff

It works, but it's pretty "young" code - there's plenty of
functionality that has yet to be coded.
* Monsters can only ride the steeds they're generated with.
* When a monster falls off a steed, it can't ever get back on.
* Monsters don't get jousting bonuses.
* Zapping and shooting effects are not symmetrical with mounted player
cases. In particular, you'll only hit one of the monsters with a wand
or spell blast, and which one depends on how elevated you are.
* I'm fairly certain that riders with kicking attacks can still use
them on the player (even though none currently exist.)
* Maybe monsters should be able to kick their steeds?
Also, quite a few noticable minor bugs are apparant, including one
concerning monster detection.

NOTE: While transcribing it I made an alteration that, though minor, is
instantly noticable - in line with players, monsters on steeds are only
displayed with their steed's glyph. Originally, it was the rider only
who was displayed. I was considering making an alteration that
recoloured the steed's glyph with the rider's colour, but that would've
caused no end of unfathomable insanity in the case of dragon riders.



